"""Long blind study (LB): pins and constants.  No logic beyond lookups and checks.

Importable without torch, numpy or the code copy.  LB continues r10 stance6 s42 from its 2,097,152 checkpoint to the
parent's own end, 12,001,280.  This file is BS2's bs_common.py (S2/r10round/bias_screen2/tools/bs_common.py, sha256
6c4c36ea...) with the root, the window (E, LENGTH, the saved pairs, the evaluation count), the validation seeds, the
continuation cap and the disk estimate changed, and the resume, stop-reason and read-schedule constants added; the
arms, the start pair, the code copy (BS's, reused read only) and the queue rules are BS2's.
Every value cites its source:
  ECS    = ecs_common.py (the pins it shares with this screen: the code copy, M1/M5, the stack, the s42 records);
  FMAN   = S1/foot/stance6/fetch/manifest.csv (F2 COPY rows, copy 1) [measured 2026-10-30 03:53 UTC by BS's
           check_inputs.py; re-measured for BS2 and for LB by check_inputs.py: FMAN lines 241 / 243 for the 2,097,152
           pair];
  TASK   = BS's build task of 2026-10-30 (4 at a time at nice 10; disk floor 1.5 GB; arms control /
           critic_blind_tail3 / gae_lambda_1 / frozen_obs_norm, none chosen here);
  TASK2  = BS2's build task of 2026-10-30 (S = 2,097,152; the start pair; the code copy reused read only);
  TASK3  = LB's build task of 2026-10-30 (E = the parent's own end; LENGTH = E - S; validation seeds 9301-9341; the
           resume of a crashed continuation from its latest complete saved pair; RR-1; process I1);
  AUTH2  = the maintainer's choice of 2026-10-30 16:23 UTC (RUNLOG line 799, "Long blind run to 12M (Recommended)"):
           continue s42 from 2,097,152 to the full 12M, 4 runs (mostly critic_blind_tail3 plus a normal control);
  PARENT = the parent's F2 records [measured by validate/parent_schedule.py, validate/logs/parent_schedule.out].
The intervention and the queue are NOT here: they are <LB>/SCREEN.json, written when the criteria are reviewed, and
pinned by sha256 in <LB>/APPROVED (screen_sha256) with the criteria and these tools.  (In this file and the other LB
tools "<BS>" means the study's own root, LB.)
"""
